{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[],"dockerImageVersionId":28755,"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# E-commerce Sales & Customer Analytics with SQL\n\n**Tools:** Google BigQuery (SQL), Python, Pandas, Matplotlib  \n**Dataset:** TheLook eCommerce — Public Synthetic Dataset\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis project analyzes e-commerce transaction data using SQL and Python, with a focus on sales performance, product category profitability, and customer purchasing behavior.\n\nThe analysis emphasizes reliable KPI definitions, data validation, reusable SQL transformations, and clear interpretation of business metrics.\n\n## Key Analytical Questions\n\n1. How has fulfilled-status order value changed over time, and what drives those changes?\n2. Which **product categories** contribute the most sales value and estimated gross profit?\n3. How do returned and cancelled order statuses affect category-level monetary exposure?\n4. How do purchasing frequency and retention patterns vary across customer groups?\n\n## Analytical Approach\n\nThe project begins with source-data validation and the development of a reusable order-level analytical model. It then applies SQL aggregation, conditional calculations, window functions, and time-based comparisons to investigate sales, products, and customer behavior.\n\n## Data Limitations\n\nTheLook is a **synthetic dataset**. Findings are intended to demonstrate analytical methodology rather than establish real-world business performance. Order statuses are observed at query time, and monetary measures do not represent verified accounting revenue.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd \nfrom google.cloud import bigquery\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n# set up client object\nclient = bigquery.Client()\n\ndataset = client.get_dataset('bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce')","metadata":{"_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.103873Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.104708Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.441356Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.104676Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.440531Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Using Kaggle's public dataset BigQuery integration.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":144},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 1. Data Understanding & Exploration\n\n## 1.1 Dataset Overview\n\n**Objective:** Explore the structure of the TheLook eCommerce dataset, identify relevant tables, and understand the data relationships before building analytical models.\n\nThis project uses the **TheLook eCommerce public synthetic dataset**, hosted on Google BigQuery. The dataset contains seven interconnected tables covering e-commerce transactions, customers, products, inventory, and website activity.\n\nThe analysis primarily focuses on four tables:\n\n| Table | Description | Analytical Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `orders` | Order records, customer identifiers, timestamps, and order statuses | Sales performance and order-level KPIs |\n| `order_items` | Individual order-item records and sale prices | Monetary calculations and transaction analysis |\n| `products` | Product categories, attributes, and unit costs | Category performance and estimated profitability |\n| `users` | Customer profiles and acquisition attributes | Customer behavior and segmentation |\n\n**Analysis Scope**\n\n- **Data source:** `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce`\n- **Reporting cutoff:** September 30, 2026\n- **Date basis:** Order creation date (`orders.created_at`)\n- **Order statuses:** All statuses are retained during data preparation and classified for KPI calculations.\n\nThe following exploration focuses on `orders` and `order_items`, which serve as the foundation of the order-level analytical model.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# Explore available tables in the dataset\n\ntables_query = \"\"\"\nSELECT\n    table_name\nFROM `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES`\nWHERE table_type = 'BASE TABLE'\nORDER BY table_name\n\"\"\"\n\ndataset_tables = client.query(tables_query).to_dataframe()\n\ndataset_tables\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.442832Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.443221Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-09T15:24:52.812055Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-09T15:24:51.443196Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-09T15:24:52.811289Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/google/cloud/bigquery/table.py:2086: UserWarning: BigQuery Storage module not found, fetch data with the REST endpoint instead.\n  warnings.warn(\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":145,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"             table_name\n0  distribution_centers\n1                events\n2       inventory_items\n3           order_items\n4                orders\n5              products\n6                 users","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>table_name</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n   