ta":{}}],"execution_count":153},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Order Items Table Preview\n\nThe `order_items` table contains individual items associated with customer orders. Each item has its own identifier, product reference, and recorded sale price.\n\nTo illustrate the relationship between the two transactional tables, the following query selects a small set of orders containing multiple items.\n\nThis example helps demonstrate why item-level values must be aggregated before constructing an order-level analytical model.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# Preview multiple items belonging to the same orders\n\norder_items_sample_query = \"\"\"\nWITH sample_orders AS (\n    SELECT\n        order_id\n    FROM `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.orders`\n\n    WHERE DATE(created_at) <= DATE '2026-09-30'\n      AND num_of_item > 1\n\n    ORDER BY created_at, order_id\n    LIMIT 3\n)\n\nSELECT\n    oi.order_id,\n    oi.id AS order_item_id,\n    oi.product_id,\n    oi.sale_price\n\nFROM `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.order_items` AS oi\n\nINNER JOIN sample_orders AS s\n    ON oi.order_id = s.order_id\n\nORDER BY oi.order_id, oi.id\n\"\"\"\n\norder_items_sample = client.query(\n    order_items_sample_query\n).to_dataframe()\n\norder_items_sample\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-09T15:25:00.975508Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-09T15:25:00.975749Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-09T15:25:02.081433Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-09T15:25:00.975725Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-09T15:25:02.080702Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/google/cloud/bigquery/table.py:2086: UserWarning: BigQuery Storage module not found, fetch data with the REST endpoint instead.\n  warnings.warn(\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":154,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"   order_id  order_item_id  product_id  sale_price\n0      9583       