4744Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":171},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Key Findings — Category Sales Performance\n\n**1. Sales value is concentrated in several leading categories.**\n\nOuterwear & Coats generated the highest fulfilled-status item value at approximately **$672.9K**, representing **12.51%** of the total, followed by Jeans at approximately **$632.7K (11.76%)**.\n\nTogether, these two categories accounted for approximately **24.27%** of total fulfilled-status item value.\n\n**2. Higher item volume does not necessarily translate into higher monetary contribution.**\n\nAlthough Jeans recorded more fulfilled items (**6,350**) than Outerwear & Coats (**4,502**), Outerwear & Coats generated greater total item value.\n\nThis difference was associated with a substantially higher average selling price for Outerwear & Coats (**$149.47**) compared with Jeans (**$99.64**), illustrating how average selling price and sales volume jointly determine category-level monetary contribution.\n\n**3. Sales contribution alone does not indicate profitability.**\n\nCategory-level monetary contribution reflects both the quantity of items sold and their average selling prices. However, higher sales value does not necessarily imply higher profitability, as product costs and margins may differ across categories.\n\nThe following section incorporates estimated product costs to evaluate gross profit and gross margin, providing a more comprehensive perspective on category performance.\n\n*Note: Findings are based on synthetic transaction data and describe observed fulfilled-status item values rather than real-world consumer demand. Fulfilled-status item value is an operational proxy, not audited recognized revenue.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 4.2.2 Category Profitability Analysis\n\n**Objective:** Evaluate product category performance using estimated gross profit and gross margin, complementing the sales-value analysis in Section 4.2.1.\n\nWhile sales value indicates the monetary contribution of each category, it does not account for product costs. This section incorporates product cost information to estimate profitability across categories.\n\n**Key Metrics**\n\n| Metric | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| Total Sale Value | Sum of recorded sale prices for fulfilled-status order items |\n| Total Product Cost | Sum of product unit costs associated with those items |\n| Estimated Gross Profit | Total Sale Value − Total Product Cost |\n| Estimated Gross Margin (%) | Estimated Gross Profit / Total Sale Value × 100 |\n| Gross Profit Contribution (%) | Category Estimated Gross Profit / Total Estimated Gross Profit × 100 |\n| Estimated Gross Profit per Item | Category Estimated Gross Profit / Items Sold |\n\n**Methodology**\n\nThe analysis joins `order_items`, `orders`, and `products`, retaining orders created on or before September 30, 2026, with statuses of `Complete` or `Shipped`.\n\nEstimated gross profit is first calculated at the order-item level and subsequently aggregated by product category.\n\n**Important Limitation**\n\nThe `products.cost` field is used as an estimated unit cost rather than verified historical cost of goods sold. The resulting profit estimates exclude additional expenses such as shipping, handling, returns processing, and other operating costs. Therefore, these metrics should not be interpreted as verified accounting profitability.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# Validate item-level data used for profitability analysis\n\nitems_validation_query = \"\"\"\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_items,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT oi.id) AS unique_items,\n\n    COUNTIF(p.id IS NULL) AS missing_product_matches,\n    COUNTIF(p.cost IS NULL) AS missing_unit_cost,\n    COUNTIF(oi.sale_price IS NULL) AS missing_sale_price\n\nFROM `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.order_items` AS oi\n\nINNER JOIN `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.orders` AS o\n    ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n\nLEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.products` AS p\n    ON oi.product_id = p.id\n\nWHERE DATE(o.created_at) <= DATE '2026-09-30'\n  AND o.status IN ('Complete', 'Shipped')\n\"\"\"\n\nitems_validation_results = client.query(\n    items_validation_query\n).to_dataframe()\n\nitems_validation_results\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-09T15:25:15.536774Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-09T15:25:15.537153Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-09T15:25:16.341983Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-09T15:25:15.537126Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-09T15:25:16.341262Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/google/cloud/bigquery/table.py:2086: UserWarning: BigQuery Storage module not found, fetch data with the REST endpoint instead.\n  warnings.warn(\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":172,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"   total_items  unique_items  missing_product_matches  missing_unit_cost  \\\n0        90486         90486                        0                  0   \n\n   missing_sale_price  \n0                   0  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>total_items</th>\n      <th>unique_items</th>\n      <th>missing_product_matches</th>\n      <th>missing_unit_cost</th>\n      <th>missing_sale_price</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>90486</td>\n      <td>90486</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":172},{"cell_type":"code","source":"category_performance_query = \"\"\"\nWITH item_profit AS (\n    SELECT\n        p.category,\n        oi.sale_price,\n        p.cost AS unit_cost,\n\n        -- Calculate estimated gross profit per item\n        oi.sale_price - p.cost AS item_gross_profit\n        \n\n    FROM `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.order_items` AS oi\n        INNER JOIN `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.orders` AS o\n            ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n            \n        LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.products` AS p\n            ON oi.product_id = p.id\n    WHERE\n        DATE(o.created_at) <= DATE '2026-09-30'\n            \n        AND\n        o.status IN ('Complete','Shipped')    \n),\ncategory_profit AS (\n    SELECT\n        category,\n\n        COUNT(*) AS item_sold,\n\n        SUM(sale_price) AS total_sale_value,\n\n        SUM(unit_cost) AS total_product_cost,\n\n        SUM(item_gross_profit) AS estimated_gp\n        \n    FROM item_profit\n    GROUP BY category\n)\n\n\nSELECT\n    category,\n    item_sold,\n    total_sale_value,\n    total_product_cost,\n    estimated_gp,\n\n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n            estimated_gp,\n            total_sale_value\n        ), 2\n    ) AS gross_margin_pct,\n\n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n            estimated_gp,\n            SUM(estimated_gp) OVER()\n        ), 2\n    ) AS gross_profit_share_pct,\n\n    ROUND(\n        SAFE_DIVIDE(\n            estimated_gp,\n            item_sold\n        ), 2\n    ) AS estimated_gp_per_item\n\nFROM category_profit\n\nORDER BY estimated_gp DESC\nLIMIT 10\n\n\"\"\"\n\ncategory_performance = client.query(category_performance_query).to_dataframe()\ncategory_performance\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-09T15:25:16.342986Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-09T15:25:16.343209Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-09T15:25:17.457616Z","shell.exe