espite contributing less total estimated gross profit.\n\n**2. Sales value and profitability are not interchangeable.**\n\nJeans generated approximately $632.7 K in fulfilled-status item value and $294.15K in estimated gross profit, with a gross margin of 46.49%.\n\nBy comparison, Suits & Sport Coats generated lower item value of approximately $314.4K but achieved a higher estimated gross margin of 59.92%.\n\nThese results illustrate the importance of examining both absolute profit contribution and relative margins when comparing category performance.\n\n**3. Methodological limitations restrict business interpretation.**\n\nThe estimates are based on recorded item sale prices and product costs from a synthetic dataset. They do not represent verified historical gross profit or account for all relevant expenses.\n\nThe findings therefore demonstrate the analytical value of integrating sales and cost data, rather than supporting direct merchandising or pricing decisions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 4.2.3 Returns & Cancellation Exposure Analysis\n\n**Objective:** Evaluate the proportion of recorded item value associated with returned and cancelled orders across product categories.\n\nThis analysis complements category sales and profitability metrics by examining order-status-related monetary exposure.\n\n**Key Metrics**\n\n| Metric | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| Returned-Status Item Share (%) | Items belonging to returned orders / All recorded items within the category × 100 |\n| Cancelled-Status Item Share (%) | Items belonging to cancelled orders / All recorded items within the category × 100 |\n| Returned Value Share (%) | Item value associated with returned orders / Total recorded item value within the category × 100 |\n| Cancelled Value Share (%) | Item value associated with cancelled orders / Total recorded item value within the category × 100 |\n| Returned Value Contribution (%) | Category returned-status item value / Total returned-status item value across all categories × 100 |\n\n**Methodology**\n\nThe analysis joins `order_items`, `orders`, and `products` at the order-item level, including orders created on or before September 30, 2026.\n\nAll order statuses are retained in the denominator to calculate category-level item and monetary shares consistently.\n\nA category-level CTE aggregates item counts and recorded values by order status, while the final SELECT calculates the corresponding percentages and contributions.\n\n**Important Distinction**\n\nThe `Returned` and `Cancelled` statuses are recorded at the order level. Therefore, these metrics describe the recorded item value associated with orders in those statuses, not confirmed item-level returns, refund amounts, or realized financial losses.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"return_cancelled_category_sql = \"\"\"\n\nWITH category_exposure AS(\n\n    SELECT\n        p.category AS category,\n        \n        COUNT(*) AS total_item_count,\n        \n        COUNTIF(o.status = 'Returned') AS returned_item_count,\n        \n        COUNTIF(o.status = 'Cancelled') AS cancelled_item_count,\n       \n        SUM(oi.sale_price) AS total_recorded_value,\n    \n        SUM(\n            CASE\n                WHEN o.status = 'Returned' THEN oi.sale_price\n                ELSE 0\n            END\n        ) AS returned_order_item_value,\n    \n\n        SUM(\n            CASE\n                WHEN o.status = 'Cancelled' THEN oi.sale_price\n                ELSE 0\n            END\n        ) AS cancelled_order_item_value,\n\n        COUNTIF(p.id IS NULL) AS missing_product_matches,\n        \n        COUNTIF(oi.sale_price IS NULL) AS missing_sale_price\n\n    FROM `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.order_items` AS oi\n        INNER JOIN `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.orders` AS o\n            ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n            \n        LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce.products` AS p\n            ON oi.product_id = p.id\n       \n    WHERE\n            DATE(o.created_at) <= DATE '2026-09-30'\n    GROUP BY category\n\n\n)\n\n\nSELECT\n    *,\n    \n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n            returned_item_count,\n            total_item_count\n        ),2\n    ) AS returned_item_share_pct,\n\n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n            cancelled_item_count,\n            total_item_count\n        ),2\n    ) AS cancelled_item_share_pct,\n\n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n           returned_order_item_value,\n           total_recorded_value\n        ),2\n    ) AS returned_value_share_pct,\n    \n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n           cancelled_order_item_value,\n           total_recorded_value\n        ),2\n    ) AS cancelled_value_share_pct,\n\n    \n    ROUND(\n        100 * SAFE_DIVIDE(\n            returned_order_item_value,\n            SUM(returned_order_item_value) OVER()\n        ), 2\n    ) AS returned_value_contribution_pct\n    \n        \n        \n    FROM category_exposure\n\n    ORDER BY returned_order_item_value DESC\n    \n\"\"\"\nreturn_cancelled_category =client.query(return_cancelled_category_sql).to_dataframe()\nreturn_cancelled_category.head()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-09T15:25:17.458712Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-09T15:25:17.459422Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-09T15:25:18.324138Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-09T15:25:17.459394Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-09T15:25:18.323259Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/google/cloud/bigquery/table.py:2086: UserWarning: BigQuery Storage module not found, fetch data with the REST endpoint instead.\n  warnings.warn(\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":174,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"                        category  total_item_count  returned_item_count  \\\n0              Outerwear & Coats              8170                  837   \n